# AI Literacy Skills, Elementary

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2, 1fr); gap:16px; max-width:900px; margin:20px auto; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">

<!-- Skill 1 -->
<div style="background:#F4FBFE; border:1px solid #CFEAF5; border-radius:10px; padding:18px;">
<div style="font-size:18px; font-weight:700; color:#0284B7; margin-bottom:10px;">
🔍 1. Recognize AI
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; margin-bottom:12px;">
Students can identify when AI is being used and describe, in simple terms, how it works.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555;">
<strong>Example:</strong> A 3rd-grade student notices that a video platform recommends new videos based on what they watched before.
</div>
</div>

<!-- Skill 2 -->
<div style="background:#F4FBFE; border:1px solid #CFEAF5; border-radius:10px; padding:18px;">
<div style="font-size:18px; font-weight:700; color:#0284B7; margin-bottom:10px;">
✅ 2. Evaluate AI Outputs
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; margin-bottom:12px;">
Students critically assess AI-generated content before accepting or using it.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555;">
<strong>Example:</strong> A 5th-grade class compares AI answers about the solar system with their science textbook to identify mistakes or missing details.
</div>
</div>

<!-- Skill 3 -->
<div style="background:#F7F4FC; border:1px solid #DDD6F3; border-radius:10px; padding:18px;">
<div style="font-size:18px; font-weight:700; color:#7A6FA6; margin-bottom:10px;">
⚙️ 3. Understand How AI Learns
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; margin-bottom:12px;">
Students understand, at an age-appropriate level, how AI systems learn from data and patterns.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555;">
<strong>Example:</strong> A 4th-grade class sorts animal pictures and discusses how AI needs many examples to learn patterns.
</div>
</div>

<!-- Skill 4 -->
<div style="background:#F7F4FC; border:1px solid #DDD6F3; border-radius:10px; padding:18px;">
<div style="font-size:18px; font-weight:700; color:#7A6FA6; margin-bottom:10px;">
✍️ 4. Use AI Responsibly
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; margin-bottom:12px;">
Students use AI to support their learning while maintaining ownership, effort, and judgment.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555;">
<strong>Example:</strong> A 5th-grade student uses AI to brainstorm story ideas, then chooses their own idea and writes the final draft themselves.
</div>
</div>

<!-- Skill 5 -->
<div style="background:#F7F8FA; border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; padding:18px;">
<div style="font-size:18px; font-weight:700; color:#555; margin-bottom:10px;">
🤔 5. Decide When to Use AI
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; margin-bottom:12px;">
Students determine whether AI is appropriate for a given task and learning goal.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555;">
<strong>Example:</strong> A 4th-grade student uses AI to check spelling but not to generate ideas for a personal narrative.
</div>
</div>

<!-- Skill 6 -->
<div style="background:#F7F8FA; border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; padding:18px;">
<div style="font-size:18px; font-weight:700; color:#555; margin-bottom:10px;">
🌎 6. Consider AI's Impact
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; margin-bottom:12px;">
Students explore how AI affects people, communities, and the world around them.
</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555;">
<strong>Example:</strong> A 5th-grade class discusses why it is unfair when AI describes doctors as men and nurses as women.
</div>
</div>

</div>
MARKDOWN
